# Keep the build context lean and predictable regardless of what sits under
# tmp/. The web image only needs the Go source of whiterabbit and scope
# (go.mod/go.sum + cmd/internal/pkg), plus web/ and runner/.
**/.git

# scope's Rails app is not needed to build the scope Go binary; excluding it
# also keeps a full local scope checkout (with web/vendor/bundle) out of the
# context.
tmp/scope/web

# Never ship the host's bundle/tmp/logs/node_modules into the context.
web/vendor/bundle
web/tmp
web/log
web/node_modules

# Never send local credentials to BuildKit, even when no Dockerfile currently
# copies their containing directory. The per-environment secrets/dev and
# secrets/prod directories collapsed into a single secrets/ holding the
# operator's live provider API keys, so the whole directory is excluded with
# carve-outs for the checked-in documentation and inert examples.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/
!secrets/README.md
!secrets/examples/

# config/master.key is gitignored, so CI clones never have it and the images CI
# builds never contained it — but a build from a developer's working tree copied
# it in via `COPY web/ ./` as root:root 0600. Rails 8.1 reads
# Rails.application.credentials before falling back to generate_local_secret in
# development, so the file merely existing made every service that boots Rails as
# uid 1000 (assistant-token-init, assistant-events) die in Errno::EACCES on it.
# Nothing in the app reads Rails credentials and production passes SECRET_KEY_BASE
# through the environment, so the key never belongs in the context.
web/config/master.key
